WEBVTT

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:02.261
You've saved a snapshot from Traffic.

00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:06.756
Now use those captured requests to test a
running copy of your service.

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:10.740
Open Snapshots, select your snapshot, and
click Replay.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.754
This is the same Orders API demo snapshot
from the Traffic View walkthrough.

00:00:16.319 --> 00:00:20.004
Choose the cluster and namespace where your
test workload is running.

00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:22.783
Then select a test config, which controls

00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:26.281
how the requests are sent and how the run
is evaluated.

00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:29.035
Select the inbound requests you want

00:00:29.035 --> 00:00:31.806
Speedscale to send to the service under
test.

00:00:31.976 --> 00:00:34.790
These are the requests your clients
originally sent.

00:00:34.961 --> 00:00:38.495
Check that the target is the staging
workload you want to test.

00:00:39.052 --> 00:00:43.939
Select the outbound dependencies you want
Speedscale to answer from the recording.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.546
Here, we attach the recorded pricing API
calls to the orders workload.

00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:51.428
Review the selection and launch the replay.

00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:53.278
The report updates as it runs.

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:55.324
When it finishes, check the outcome.

00:00:55.494 --> 00:01:00.547
This example report shows where to open
Accuracy for assertion differences and

00:01:00.547 --> 00:01:04.239
Mocked Responses to see whether dependency
calls matched.

00:01:04.785 --> 00:01:08.091
Run the same snapshot again when you have a
new build to check.
